From 4796fbc752cb3dc90a45a29f00672bc20fa34602 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: ipa: soft: Make the AGC loop parameters tunable

The soft ISP AGC hardcodes its target, hysteresis, proportional gain and
maximum per-frame step. The right values are not universal: the loop gain
that converges nicely on one sensor overshoots on another, because how far
the exposure moves before the change takes effect depends on how many
frames that sensor takes to apply it. On the IMX345 a bright scene drives
the loop past the target and into clipping, which turns blown highlights
green.

Adjust, BlackLevel and Ccm already take their parameters from the tuning
file; Agc is the only soft ISP algorithm that does not. Give it the same
init() hook and read the four values from tuning data, keeping the current
constants as defaults so a bare "- Agc:" behaves exactly as before.
---
 src/ipa/softisp/algorithms/agc.cpp | 255 +++++++++++++++++++++--------
 src/ipa/softisp/algorithms/agc.h   |  20 +--
 2 files changed, 199 insertions(+), 76 deletions(-)

